# serve.py is the local no-store dev server. On a static host it is not a server
# at all, just a .py file people can download, so it does not ship.
serve.py
__pycache__/

# test/ DOES ship. It is the port's own harness and the generator for the share
# card, and the page claims its numbers come from the build — a reader who wants
# to check that should be able to read portcheck.mjs rather than take it on
# trust. robots.txt keeps it out of search results, which is the right treatment
# for evidence: reachable, not indexed.

# The Vercel CLI already skips .env* and .vercel by hardcoded default, but a
# credential's exclusion belongs declared in the repo, not inherited from a
# tool's invisible defaults — .env.local here holds the CLI's own OIDC token.
.env*
.vercel
